ability","define_subjective_and_objective_image_quality_for_the_intended_screen_or_print_size_and crop","use_optical_aberration_and_shutter_lag_as_test_dimensions_not_as_diagnoses_or_fixed_results_for_an_exact listing","keep_each_community_report_at_its_author_phone_task_skill_output_and_time scope","compare_one_verified_exact_camera_with_the_mothers_actual_current_phone_not_with_a_generic_or_different_high_end phone","verify_current_model_variant_condition_lens_battery_charger_card_cables_transfer_path_warranty_returns_shipping_and_delivered cost","observe_the_mother_operating_both_devices_for_static_garden_backlit_indoor_moving_grandchild_and_flash_or_no_flash tasks","match_scenes_framing_and_final_output_size_and_mask_or_randomize_device_labels_where practical","record_time_to_first_shot_focus_and_timing_success_keeper_rate_image_preference_transfer_charging_errors_carry_burden_and_total_cost separately","predeclare_usability_keeper_output_workflow_condition_returnability_and_cost thresholds_and_mark_each_pass_fail_or unresolved","do_not_let_a_rating_low_price_technical_term_phone_anecdote_or_one_sharp_crop_compensate_for_a_failed_hard gate","buy_only_a_verified_returnable_camera_that_passes_all_recipient_matched_gates_and_meaningfully_beats_the_actual_phone_otherwise_improve_the_phone_workflow_choose_printing_support_rerun_or defer"],"scenario":"You are considering an inexpensive compact camera as a gift for your mother, who wants simple garden and grandchildren snapshots. Frozen seller pages show a Sony DSC-W80 old-model offer at 49.95 dollars with a 91-percent aggregate over eleven reviews, an HP M447 camera-and-printer offer at 60.61 dollars with a 100-percent aggregate over four reviews, a Canon ELPH 300 HS at 129.95 dollars with an 82-percent aggregate over twelve reviews, a Kodak DX4530 at 47.45 dollars with a 75-percent aggregate over twelve reviews, and a Sony W800 accessory bundle at 199 dollars with a 78-percent aggregate over twelve reviews. The pages do not establish current delivered condition, review distribution, reviewer scenes, battery or accessory state, return rights, recipient usability or performance against her actual phone. Background sources discuss point-and-shoot simple-operation intent, star scales, self-selection, user-task usability tests, subjective and objective image quality, optical aberration, shutter lag and user versus professional review authorship. Community pages include one positive phone-camera report, one processing complaint and one task-specific request for an older phone. No source contains a representative reviewer sample, a same-scene recipient test, an exact lens diagnosis or a universal compact-versus-phone winner.","target":"Determine which parts of the favorable seller feedback and the enthusiast criticism are actually applicable to this mother and exact gift choice rather than declaring one crowd correct. Audit the five exact seller aggregates and their unknown review populations, explain the difference between point-and-shoot design intent and observed usability, and translate image-quality, lens-aberration and shutter-lag criticism into declared scenes, outputs and measurements. Keep all phone reports scoped. Build a claim-to-task table showing device, reviewer population, scene, output, metric and threshold; then specify exact-offer verification and the smallest practical mother-operated same-scene trial against her actual phone, including garden, backlight, indoor and moving-grandchild tasks, normalized screen or print outputs, separate usability, timing, keeper, preference and workflow metrics, and predeclared pass, fail or unresolved gates. End with a conditional buy, improve-phone, printing-support, corrected-trial or deferral rule and no universal retailer, enthusiast, compact-camera or phone winner."},"graph_motif":"multi_branch_synthesis","graph_node_to_step_id":{"bridge_camera_decision_preparation":"B8","bridge_community_phone_scope":"B1","bridge_feedback_recon